%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 0ca23d3e41cd5424c9ec72c610ef25a4, type: 3}
  m_Name: DetectiveMonika_checkBody
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  autoFocusSpeaker: 1
  screens:
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: I'd like to check the body myself.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118809755189332
    - rid: 1790118809755189337
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 89f7d0b97106b6448939eb57dd9aa235, type: 2}
    dialog: Yes, captain.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118809755189341
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118809755189344
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 89f7d0b97106b6448939eb57dd9aa235, type: 2}
    dialog: This is where Anoriath was murdered-
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118809755189345
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 89f7d0b97106b6448939eb57dd9aa235, type: 2}
    dialog: His bed is on our right, while Elrindir's is on our left.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Yeah, I could assume based off of the blood stains...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118809755189346
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Wait, so was the body found in bed?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118809755189347
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 89f7d0b97106b6448939eb57dd9aa235, type: 2}
    dialog: Yes, I took him out of the bed to examine the body.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118809755189348
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: (Which means that there probably wasn't a struggle, and Anoriath was
      killed in his sleep.)
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Let's get a closer look at the body...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118809755189349
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118809755189351
    - rid: 1790118809755189352
    - rid: 1790118809755189353
    - rid: 1790118809755189354
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Hm...
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: The stabs wounds don't seem very big, they must've been made by something
      thin...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118809755189355
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: -!
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118809755189356
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Ivar, did you notice the slit drawn across his neck?
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118809755189357
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 89f7d0b97106b6448939eb57dd9aa235, type: 2}
    dialog: Oh, no I didn't. Good eye.
    ScreenActions: []
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: The width of the cut isn't drastically smaller than the stab wounds...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118809755189358
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: I feel like it would be safe to assume that the stabs and the cut were
      made by the same thing.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118809755189359
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 89f7d0b97106b6448939eb57dd9aa235, type: 2}
    dialog: Both seem to be dagger-sized.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118809755189360
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: So our murder weapon is probably a dagger, then.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118809755189361
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Which, now that I'm thinking about it, probably doesn't narrow down our
      suspect pool.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118809755189362
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Regardless, since there was no fight between the two, we can probably
      assume that he was killed by the slit to the neck specifically.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118809755189363
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: 'Which raises the question: "why stab the body after it''s already dead?"'
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118809755189364
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 89f7d0b97106b6448939eb57dd9aa235, type: 2}
    dialog: It would make sense if the murderer committed the crime out of hatred
      or passion.
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118809755189365
  - speaker: {fileID: 11400000, guid: bcc4aa0537be91d488c1075e0cd8d29a, type: 2}
    dialog: Maybe...
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118809755189366
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions:
    - rid: 1790118809755189367
    - rid: 1790118809755189368
    - rid: 1790118809755189369
    - rid: 1790118809755189370
  - speaker: {fileID: 0}
    dialog: 
    ScreenActions: []
